[src/Databases/DatabaseRemote.cpp:outdated] The loading regression is still present for stored `AS remote(...)` / `AS remoteSecure(...)` tables. At the current head, `src/TableFunctions/TableFunctionRemote.cpp:30-31` calls `parseRemoteFunctionArguments` without `limit_total_addresses`, so it remains `true`. Startup reaches this call through `factory.get` in `src/Databases/DatabaseOnDisk.cpp:149`, before the cached columns or lazy storage proxy are used; it never reaches the exemption in `registerStorageRemote`.

A minimal regression case is the table-function version of the new test:

```sql
SET table_function_remote_max_addresses = 4;
CREATE TABLE remote_mixed_tf (dummy UInt8)
AS remote('127.0.0.{1,2}:{9000|9001}', system.one);
DETACH TABLE remote_mixed_tf;
SET table_function_remote_max_addresses = 3;
ATTACH TABLE remote_mixed_tf;
```

The last statement still takes the total-limit path and throws at four addresses, although the stored definition fits the previous per-stage limit. With a previously stored 600-shard/two-replica definition, startup likewise rejects the table at the default limit of 1000. Please carry the metadata-replay exemption into table-function argument parsing too, and cover this persisted representation in the regression test.
